  "evidence_notes": "Diagnosed 5 years ago. Also has psoriatic arthritis and depression. Symptoms started gradually, attributed to diet/stress. Blood in stool led to diagnosis. Initial treatments: mesalamine, prednisone, sulfasalazine (allergic reaction), methotrexate (nausea). Started Humira, which helps both Crohn's and psoriatic arthritis (70% improvement). Marriage counseling is ongoing due to strain. Children (5 and 3) don't understand. Work is fully remote. Medical costs are growing ($10k/year out-of-pocket). Concerns about finances and future biologic failures. Support group exists but mostly women; found online group for dads with chronic illness. Worried about biologic failure and future surgery with young kids."
